[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Level 3 of the V-model, the hardware branch, parallel to
[`03_software_req.sdoc`](03_software_req.sdoc). Both refine `SYS-`.

`SYS-HW-*` in [`02_system_req.sdoc`](02_system_req.sdoc) says what the system
needs: two switching devices in series, a buzzer, an interlock input. These
are the board-level consequences, with the numbers. A requirement is here when
getting it wrong is a hardware change rather than a firmware one.

Verification: **I** inspection or review, **A** analysis or calculation,
**T** bench measurement, **H** on the HIL fixture.

Each item's open work is tracked in section A of
[`tasklist.md`](../tasklist.md); this document is what the board has to achieve,
not the list of fixes outstanding.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
UID: SECT-HW-1
TITLE: 1. Heat authority

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HWR-01
TITLE: Charge-pump release inside one second
STATEMENT: >>>
The charge pump shall release the contactor within **1 s** of `HEAT_EN` ceasing to toggle, and shall pass through the MOSFET's linear region fast enough that the contactor cannot rest partially closed.

Present circuit: `HEAT_EN` → R19 → C23 (10 µF) → D5 (BAT54S) → `HEAT_EN_DC` → C24 (3.3 µF) ∥ R20 (47 k) → Q3 gate. Two numbers need establishing rather than assuming: the pumped level is about 3.3 V − 2·V<sub>f</sub> ≈ 2.7 V, below the 4.5 V at which the AO3400A's R<sub>DS(on)</sub> is specified; and decay is τ ≈ 155 ms, so release is a slide rather than an edge.

This is the circuit [LINK: SYS-SAF-02] rests on and the design's most fragile idea. If the margin is thin, a comparator or a retriggerable monostable buys a crisp threshold for a few cents.
<<<
PRIORITY: M
VERIFICATION: A, H
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-HW-07
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-SAF-02
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HWR-02
TITLE: Outputs default to de-energised
STATEMENT: >>>
Every heater and contactor control output shall carry an external pull-down to the de-energised state, and shall avoid strapping pins and pins that glitch during reset.

The window this covers is reset to first instruction, where a GPIO is high-impedance and the net sits wherever the board leaks to.
<<<
PRIORITY: M
VERIFICATION: I, T
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-HW-08
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HWR-03
TITLE: The supervisor's permit needs its own pull-down
STATEMENT: >>>
The supervisor's permit output is active high, so its series element shall have an external pull-down. Without one there is a window at every supervisor reset in which the element's state is whatever the board leaks to.
<<<
PRIORITY: M
VERIFICATION: I, T
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-HW-26
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HWR-04
TITLE: Freewheel across the coil
STATEMENT: >>>
The coil's freewheel diode shall sit across the coil itself, on the kiln side of every series interrupting element, so opening any of them leaves the current a path to decay through.

Referenced to the raw supply instead, the inductive transient appears across the opening contacts and erodes the lid switch.
<<<
PRIORITY: M
VERIFICATION: I
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-HW-25
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: SECT-HW-2
TITLE: 2. Temperature acquisition

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HWR-05
TITLE: Separate buses for the two front ends
STATEMENT: >>>
The chamber MAX31856 shall be on the supervisor's SPI bus and the enclosure one on the controller's. Neither shall share a bus, a chip select or a `~DRDY` line with the other.

A supervisor whose chamber reading can be disturbed by the controller's bus traffic, or whose chip select can be driven by a controller that has crashed with a pin latched, is not independent of it.
<<<
PRIORITY: M
VERIFICATION: I
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-HW-02
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HWR-06
TITLE: Open-drain outputs are pulled up
STATEMENT: >>>
Every MAX31856 `~DRDY` and `~FAULT` output shall carry a pull-up. They are open-drain and read as asserted when floating.
<<<
PRIORITY: M
VERIFICATION: I
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-HW-02
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HWR-07
TITLE: Chip selects are defined through reset
STATEMENT: >>>
`TC1_CS` and `TC2_CS` shall be pulled to their idle level. Both float during reset and boot, and a chip select asserted by leakage starts a conversion nobody asked for.
<<<
PRIORITY: S
VERIFICATION: I
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-HW-08
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HWR-08
TITLE: Thermocouple inputs are clamped
STATEMENT: >>>
The thermocouple inputs shall be clamped to the front end's supply rails, and `VBIAS` shall be decoupled.

A thermocouple is a multi-metre unshielded pair routed beside a switching multi-kilowatt load. R24/R25 (10 k/10 k off +3V3) currently present about 5 kΩ to the bias node with no local capacitance.
<<<
PRIORITY: M
VERIFICATION: I, T
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-HW-15
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: SECT-HW-3
TITLE: 3. Current measurement

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HWR-09
TITLE: Full scale fits the ADC without clipping
STATEMENT: >>>
The CT front end shall put **60 A** ([LINK: SWR-CUR-02]'s full scale) at roughly **0.5 V<sub>rms</sub>** about the mid-rail bias, and the resulting LSB shall be recorded against the 0.1 A resolution the same requirement asks for.

J10 is annotated "CT 30 A/1 V". At 60 A that delivers 2 V<sub>rms</sub> = ±2.83 V<sub>pk</sub> about the 1.65 V bias: the clamp conducts and the reading saturates across the whole upper half of the required range. Even at 30 A the swing reaches 0.24 V to 3.06 V, where the ESP32-S3 ADC is least linear.
<<<
PRIORITY: M
VERIFICATION: A, T
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-HW-17
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HWR-10
TITLE: The anti-alias filter is below Nyquist
STATEMENT: >>>
The CT anti-alias corner shall sit **below half the sample rate**. Pick the sample rate first, then the filter.

R26 (1 k) + C25 (220 nF) gives f<sub>c</sub> ≈ 723 Hz against a 1 kHz sample rate whose Nyquist is 500 Hz: the corner is above Nyquist and the filter does not anti-alias. Either 4–8 kHz sampling with a corner near 300 Hz, or a corner near 200 Hz for 1 kHz.
<<<
PRIORITY: M
VERIFICATION: A, T
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-HW-17
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HWR-11
TITLE: An absent CT is electrically recognisable
STATEMENT: >>>
`CURR_SENSE` shall carry a defined bias that the CT winding cannot produce, so an open input is distinguishable from genuinely zero current.

With J10 open the node is held only by C25 and diode leakage, so it drifts. [LINK: SWR-CUR-11] has to tell those two cases apart and [LINK: SWR-CUR-12] refuses to start a run on the second.
<<<
PRIORITY: M
VERIFICATION: I, T
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-HW-17
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HWR-12
TITLE: The clamp holds the ADC inside its absolute maximum
STATEMENT: >>>
The CT node shall be clamped to within the ADC pin's absolute maximum of −0.3 V to V<sub>DD</sub>+0.3 V, through a series resistor that limits clamp current.

A **Schottky** clamp is required rather than preferred: at 1 mA a BAT54S drops about 0.32 V and holds the node near 3.6 V, while a silicon diode's 0.7 V would hold it at 4.0 V and exceed the pin's rating by 0.4 V. D9 is a BAT54S, which is correct; what is open is the scaling of [LINK: HWR-09], which currently drives the clamp during normal operation.
<<<
PRIORITY: M
VERIFICATION: A, I
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-HW-17
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HWR-13
TITLE: The CT is specified on the schematic
STATEMENT: >>>
The CT's required characteristics shall appear as a schematic note, and no CT-related part shall be annotated "(opt)" without the behaviour of its absence being defined.

A split-core CT fitted to the wrong conductor reads a current that is real and not the heater's.
<<<
PRIORITY: S
VERIFICATION: I
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-HW-16
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: SECT-HW-4
TITLE: 4. Power and protection

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HWR-14
TITLE: The +5 V rail is budgeted, and coil inrush does not reach the MCU
STATEMENT: >>>
The +5 V rail shall be budgeted for the contactor coil, the buzzer and the MCU together, and coil inrush shall not be able to brown out the MCU.

The coil is the largest and least constant load on the board, and the one that switches while a kiln is at temperature.
<<<
PRIORITY: M
VERIFICATION: A, T
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-HW-05
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HWR-15
TITLE: The regulator has dropout and thermal margin
STATEMENT: >>>
The 3V3 regulator shall hold regulation at the lowest input the design accepts, with its junction temperature inside its rating at full load and the highest specified ambient.

An AMS1117 at the worst case is the part to check first.
<<<
PRIORITY: M
VERIFICATION: A
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-HW-05
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HWR-16
TITLE: Input transients are clamped
STATEMENT: >>>
`V_IN` shall have transient protection. The fuse and series diode cover overcurrent and reverse polarity; neither clamps a surge, and the board sits next to a switching multi-kilowatt load.
<<<
PRIORITY: S
VERIFICATION: I
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-HW-05
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HWR-17
TITLE: USB is protected and decoupled
STATEMENT: >>>
`USB_DP`/`USB_DM` shall have low-capacitance ESD protection, and `VBUS` shall be decoupled. The data pair currently runs from the connector to the ESP32-S3's native USB pins unprotected.
<<<
PRIORITY: S
VERIFICATION: I
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-HW-05
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: SECT-HW-5
TITLE: 5. Operator interface and boot

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HWR-18
TITLE: Boot-mode and encoder inputs are defined
STATEMENT: >>>
`MCU_IO0` shall have an external pull-up, and the encoder inputs shall have a defined network whose time constant is compatible with the quadrature decoder's expectations.

IO0 is pulled to ground by SW2 with nothing holding it otherwise; R10–R12 with C20–C22 need their corner checked against the knob's fastest realistic rotation.
<<<
PRIORITY: S
VERIFICATION: I, T
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-HW-04
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HWR-19
TITLE: The supervisor's programming interface is reachable
STATEMENT: >>>
The supervisor's SWD pins shall come out to test points rather than being left as pads, and the clear button of [LINK: SYS-HW-28] shall be wired to the supervisor and to nothing else.

The independence argument rests on that firmware being reviewable and flashable on its own.
<<<
PRIORITY: M
VERIFICATION: I
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-HW-26
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HWR-20
TITLE: Test points survive the chain they outlived
STATEMENT: >>>
Each thermocouple `~FAULT` net shall retain its own test point, and the coil drive and permit nets shall each have one.

The discrete fault chain is superseded ([LINK: SYS-HW-24]); the test points cost nothing and are how a front end is diagnosed on a bench.
<<<
PRIORITY: S
VERIFICATION: I
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-HW-24
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: SECT-HW-6
TITLE: 6. Documentation and review

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HWR-21
TITLE: One pin map, generated
STATEMENT: >>>
There shall be a single pin-map artefact, derived from the schematic rather than maintained beside it, covering both microcontrollers.

Pin assignments currently live in the schematic, in `board_pins.h` and in the supervisor's README, which is three places that can disagree.
<<<
PRIORITY: M
VERIFICATION: I
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-HW-10
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HWR-22
TITLE: ERC is clean or its exclusions are recorded
STATEMENT: >>>
Electrical rule check shall pass, and every exclusion shall carry its reason in the project file. The shared SPI `SDO` is the known one.
<<<
PRIORITY: M
VERIFICATION: I
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-HW-10
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HWR-23
TITLE: Mains-adjacent routing is reviewed before fabrication
STATEMENT: >>>
The coil interrupt and every mains-adjacent net shall be reviewed for clearance and creepage before a board is ordered. The PCB currently has no tracks at all, so this is a requirement on work not yet done rather than a check on work done.
<<<
PRIORITY: M
VERIFICATION: I
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-HW-05
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]
